ttychatter C walkthrough
========================

1. Build the program
--------------------

    make

2. Store an API key
-------------------

Plaintext config:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key

Encrypted with gpg:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

The default OpenRouter config path is:

    ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config

3. Fetch model catalog
----------------------

    ./ttychatter --update-models

The default model cache is:

    ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json

4. Browse/search/select/test models
-----------------------------------

    ./ttychatter --models
    ./ttychatter --models --search free
    ./ttychatter --models --model-type routers
    ./ttychatter --routers
    ./ttychatter --select-model
    ./ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto --save

Common model-list filters:

    ./ttychatter --models --favorites-only
    ./ttychatter --models --sort context
    ./ttychatter --models --min-input-tokens 32000
    ./ttychatter --models --min-output-tokens 4096
    ./ttychatter --models --require-tokens
    ./ttychatter --models --allow-missing-tokens
    ./ttychatter --models --hide-preview
    ./ttychatter --models --show-preview
    ./ttychatter --models --all

Favorite model commands:

    ./ttychatter --favorites
    ./ttychatter --favorite-model openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --unfavorite-model openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --unbookmark-model openrouter/auto

5. Create an input file
-----------------------

    cat > input.txt
    Explain what a Unix pipeline is in one paragraph.
    Ctrl+D

6. Send one input and auto-save a timestamped session
-----------------------------------------------------

    ./ttychatter input.txt

This creates a new log under:

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/

The filename remains mechanical and timestamped, for example:

    session-2026-06-03-14-22-33.log

Equivalent one-shot forms:

    ./ttychatter --input input.txt
    ./ttychatter --prompt 'Explain what a Unix pipeline is.'
    printf 'Explain what a Unix pipeline is.\n' | ./ttychatter

7. Send input and write an explicit output/session log
------------------------------------------------------

    ./ttychatter input.txt session.log
    ./ttychatter --input input.txt --output session.log
    ./ttychatter --prompt 'Give me a tiny example.' --output session.log

This uses ./session.log exactly.  It does not move the log into SESSION_DIR.

8. Resume the same explicit session
-----------------------------------

    cat > followup.txt
    Give me a tiny example.
    Ctrl+D

    ./ttychatter followup.txt session.log

9. Use named sessions
---------------------

Bare session names resolve under the shared OpenRouter session directory:

    ./ttychatter --interactive notes
    ./ttychatter --resume notes
    ./ttychatter --session notes --prompt 'Next question'
    ./ttychatter --show-memory notes

The default path for that named session is:

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/notes.log

Use ./notes.log when the intended file is in the current directory.

10. List and retitle sessions
-----------------------------

    ./ttychatter --list
    ./ttychatter --rename-session notes Friendly Notes

The retitle operation writes session-title metadata into the log.  It does not
rename the filename.  The --list table displays the title when present and uses
the filename stem as fallback.

Automatic AI-generated titles are optional and off by default:

    ./ttychatter --set SESSION_AUTO_TITLE=1
    ./ttychatter --set SESSION_TITLE_MODEL=openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --set SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS=8

SESSION_TITLE_MODEL is a secondary model used only for title metadata.  The
main conversation still uses MODEL.

11. Start interactive mode
--------------------------

No arguments on a terminal start a new auto-saved interactive session:

    ./ttychatter
    ./ttychatter --new

Resume or name a specific interactive session:

    ./ttychatter --interactive notes
    ./ttychatter --chat notes
    ./ttychatter --session notes --interactive

12. Attach files
----------------

    ./ttychatter -a notes.txt -a image.png prompt.txt session.log

Generated long fenced code blocks are saved under:

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/

13. Use loopback output
-----------------------

    ./ttychatter --loopback prompt.txt session.log | less
    ./ttychatter --loopback-file latest-answer.txt prompt.txt session.log

14. Interactive mode with colon commands
----------------------------------------

    ./ttychatter --interactive notes

    ttychatter> hello
    ttychatter> :models
    ttychatter> :attach notes.txt
    ttychatter> :memory
    ttychatter> :rename Friendly Notes
    ttychatter> :quit

15. Check command-line help
---------------------------

    ./ttychatter --help
    ./ttychatter --version
    man ./ttychatter.1

Useful non-walkthrough flags are listed here so this file stays aligned with
--help and the man page:

    ./ttychatter --model openrouter/auto input.txt session.log
    ./ttychatter --attach notes.txt input.txt session.log
    ./ttychatter --yes input.txt session.log
    ./ttychatter --forget-api-key
    ./ttychatter --config
    ./ttychatter --set MODEL=openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --unset MODEL
    ./ttychatter --list
    ./ttychatter --edit-memory notes
    ./ttychatter --clear-memory notes
    ./ttychatter --editor-prompt
    ./ttychatter --editor-prompt session.log
    ./ttychatter --search-sessions TEXT
    ./ttychatter --search TEXT --all-sessions
    ./ttychatter --send-input enter
    ./ttychatter --theme plain
    ./ttychatter --code-attachment-min-lines 20
    ./ttychatter --doctor
    ./ttychatter --credits

16. Demo mode
-------------

Demo mode avoids network/API use:

    ./ttychatter --demo input.txt
    ./ttychatter --demo input.txt demo.log
    ./ttychatter --demo --prompt 'demo prompt'
    ./ttychatter --demo --interactive demo

Interactive parity commands
---------------------------

Inside the prompt, use colon commands for local control:

    :help
    :list
    :rename Friendly Notes
    :models
    :routers
    :update-models
    :select-model
    :test-model openrouter/auto
    :model openrouter/auto
    :model-save openrouter/auto
    :favorites
    :favorite openrouter/auto
    :unfavorite openrouter/auto
    :config
    :set KEY VALUE
    :unset KEY
    :set-api-key
    :set-api-key gpg
    :forget-api-key
    :memory
    :edit-memory
    :clear-memory
    :attach notes.txt
    :attachments
    :pending
    :clear-attachments
    :editor
    :search TEXT
    :search-all TEXT
    :credits
    :doctor
    :quit

These commands are handled by ttychatter itself and are not sent to the AI.
Use ./ttychatter --help or man ttychatter for the full command-line option list.
